## Seven-family summary and retained gains

The existing fixed-20 admission review concludes parity is not established against both controls: ordinary complete-operation losses remain in dense 512/1024, long unsafe-boundary reflow, cold mounting, width-change measurement, and small repeated setters. The draft stays held; sparse/inspection and prepared-edit gains do not cancel those losses. See the source report for the full family table and availability/calibration caveats.

